Cell[TextData[{
 "A Euclidean head is inert: it holds its points and options and computes \
nothing on its own. ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraMeasurement"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ad54887d-ff09-4ea2-b2dd-ce594584af6f"],
 " is what evaluates it, reading every property off the head's ",
 StyleBox["graph",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] a directed graph whose source-to-sink chains (or, for a closed \
head, whose directed cycles) are exactly the head's members \[LongDash] by \
one forward and one backward sweep of a dynamic-programming count, never by \
enumeration."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a5cac42b-18a9-4963-b8e1-8ed3bafc3bad"],

Cell["The properties:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2c497a07-8298-46f2-a2a5-f8600dd6d4f1"],

